{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and may not consider arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated, sealed or juvenile records; after a conditional offer only certain convictions may be weighed through an individualized assessment.","key_value":"1st degree 6 years; 2nd/3rd degree 4 years; 4th degree 1 year","coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Methamphetamine-related convictions and lifetime sex-offender registration may still be considered.","coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; drug-related methamphetamine manufacture convictions and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Penalties up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior), or $10,000 (two or more priors); director may also order cease-and-desist and corrective action.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-56","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not, either before or after the issuance of a conditional offer, evaluate an applicant based on any of the following types of criminal records: (1) arrests or charges that have not resulted in a criminal conviction; (2) expunged convictions; (3) convictions erased through executive pardon;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include review of criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require the applicant's rental application fee be returned; violations may draw penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after overturned order","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and the court overturns the director's order, the provider may evict a former applicant housed under that order, giving at least 45 days' notice before the eviction.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, except units in owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"then a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

